the deal is done the month-long saga of  who will own twitter appears over  in one of the largest and most unusual  tech acquisitions ever the board of  directors at twitter unanimously agreed  to sell the social media company to elon  musk for 44 billion dollars  up until the deal was announced there  was doubt on wall street that musk could  cobble together the financing needed but  he did  musk helped pay for the deal with 25  25.5 billion dollars in debt financing  by a group of banks led by morgan  stanley in a press release announcing  the deal musk talked about improving the  platform by getting rid of automated  spam accounts and making its algorithms  open to the public and authenticating  all users  but for musk buying twitter is about  free speech or at least his version of  it potentially ending twitter's current  content moderation or stopping  de-platforming of users who break the  rules  elon musk is not buying twitter for  financial reasons although he thinks he  can make some money on it  he's buying it for ideological reasons  and i think that's the really important  part in all this  and that's ultimately what's scary  with musk in control they fear a return  to the unruly spread of disinformation  on the platform so is today a good day  or bad day for twitter users  that is probably the most important  question here um and i think it's also  the question that's going to be hardest  to answer i think that if he undoes a  lot of the work that has been done  trying to protect against sort of  normatively bad speech such as  misinformation and especially hate  speech that's going to be a bad day for  for twitter users um but you know  there's a chance that he takes over  and doesn't sort of have quite a  sweeping of a reform agenda as he's as  he's put forth  in over the last couple of weeks  it's been a tumultuous month for twitter  that saw musk take a nine percent stake  in the company making him its largest  shareholder he was then offered a seat  on the board of directors only to have  it abruptly revoked followed by his cash  offer to buy the entire company all  within the last few weeks  ultimately elon musk got what he wanted  to not only be a twitter user but to  also be its owner  gabriel rosando al jazeera new york
 

